# Short 9, "Write your own chords" (vertical, tools/film.py --layout vertical): Fog playing; on the Dub page Drift
# down to 2 bars (a chord every two bars), then EDIT for the Chords page and four slots written, a bar each (a
# key for the root, KNOB 2 the kind, KNOB 3 the type, KNOB 1 the next slot): Gm7, EbM7, Cm7, Dm7; then the
# progression plays round. Every move from a bar's downbeat. Each `bar` prints the film's time there (the cue
# sheet for the labels).
turn PRESET 3 5
wait 30
expect piece 3
bar 8
wav 18-short-progression.wav
film 18-short-progression.film
bar 8 FOG playing (G Aeolian, 112)
bar 10 KNOB 4 on the Dub page: Drift 64 bars to 2
turn K4 -5 200
expect par6 0
bar 11 EDIT: the Chords page
tap EDIT
bar 12 slot 1: G (white 2), KNOB 3 to 7: Gm7
tapkey w1
wait 300
turn K3 2 200
bar 13 KNOB 1 to slot 2: Eb (black 5), KNOB 2 Major, KNOB 3 Maj7: EbM7
turn K1 1 200
wait 200
tapkey b4
wait 300
turn K2 -1 200
wait 200
turn K3 3 200
bar 14 slot 3: C (white 5), 7: Cm7
turn K1 1 200
wait 200
tapkey w4
wait 300
turn K3 2 200
bar 15 slot 4: D (white 6), 7: Dm7
turn K1 1 200
wait 200
tapkey w5
wait 300
turn K3 2 200
expect par88 1
expect par64 7
expect par65 3
expect par66 0
expect par67 2
bar 16 the progression, a chord every 2 bars: slot 3, Cm7
wait 300
expect chordroot 0
bar 18 slot 4, Dm7
wait 300
expect chordroot 2
bar 20 round again: slot 1, Gm7
wait 300
expect chordroot 7
bar 22 slot 2, EbM7
wait 300
expect chordroot 3
bar 24 slot 3, Cm7 (the phrase a Break: the kick and the bass out)
wait 300
expect chordroot 0
bar 26 slot 4, Dm7
bar 28 END
filmstop
wavstop
